WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.611
- You ready to talk about your emotions?

00:00:01.611 --> 00:00:03.713
- Not really. (laughs)

00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:05.442
- Every guy, no guy's been excited

00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:07.602
to talk to me about their feelings.

00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:10.435
(mid tempo music)

00:00:14.216 --> 00:00:15.700
As a man, do you feel comfortable

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.161
expressing yourself emotionally?

00:00:17.161 --> 00:00:17.994
- Not at all.

00:00:17.994 --> 00:00:19.182
- No, but sometimes, yeah.

00:00:19.182 --> 00:00:21.276
- I feel comfortable
expressing myself when I'm mad,

00:00:21.276 --> 00:00:24.933
but not like, emotionally,
like, oh, I feel feelings, no.

00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:25.766
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

00:00:25.766 --> 00:00:28.180
- I do, yeah, I totally feel comfortable.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.666
- Uh, yes.

00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:31.245
Sometimes it depends on the emotion.

00:00:31.245 --> 00:00:32.868
- Tristan's a Cancer, he told me this.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.311
- Yeah.
- So it makes a lot of sense.

00:00:34.311 --> 00:00:37.755
- Because of the man I am,
a man of trans experience,

00:00:37.755 --> 00:00:41.424
I actually oddly feel more
comfortable expressing myself

00:00:41.424 --> 00:00:43.943
as a man than I did before I transitioned.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.452
I felt like I had nothing to prove

00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:48.564
and I could be as emotional
as I wanted to be.

00:00:48.564 --> 00:00:50.944
- I think it's a fear of
like, being vulnerable.

00:00:50.944 --> 00:00:53.149
- So you would say like crying,
you don't feel comfortable--

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:54.564
- I don't cry in front of people.

00:00:54.564 --> 00:00:55.826
- When was the last time you cried?

00:00:55.826 --> 00:00:57.138
- Probably like a year ago.

00:00:57.138 --> 00:00:59.576
- Yeah, I don't remember
the last time I cried.

00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:00.498
- Have you cried this year at all?

00:01:00.498 --> 00:01:02.412
Do you think you've cried this year?

00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:04.745
- I don't know, I don't think so.

00:01:04.745 --> 00:01:06.463
- Intense shit, I won't cry,

00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:08.147
I'm stoic as fuck, I don't care.

00:01:08.147 --> 00:01:10.701
It's like I intellectualize everything.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:13.485
- When I cry I don't just
like, medium cry, I ugly cry.

00:01:13.485 --> 00:01:14.627
- But that's okay, 'cause you're getting

00:01:14.627 --> 00:01:16.256
them feelings out, though!
- No, no!

00:01:16.256 --> 00:01:18.239
- I didn't want, I just want that like...

00:01:18.239 --> 00:01:20.246
I want that one tear.
- That one tear?

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.728
I just want the one tear.
- That thug tear.

00:01:21.728 --> 00:01:22.766
Jared wants a thug tear.

00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:24.069
- Yeah, I want a thug tear.

00:01:24.069 --> 00:01:27.253
- I cried when I went to
Hong Kong for six months.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.420
That was 2010.

00:01:29.491 --> 00:01:30.324
(laughs)

00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:33.768
- It's not, it's like not
okay to feel vulnerable,

00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:37.005
so I'm already conditioned
since I was a kid

00:01:37.005 --> 00:01:39.005
that men do not cry, so.

00:01:39.985 --> 00:01:42.702
And the problem with that
is now I have a problem

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.188
being vulnerable in front of people.

00:01:44.188 --> 00:01:46.605
(jazz music)

00:01:47.485 --> 00:01:51.425
- Professor Ad Vingerhoets
of Tilburg University

00:01:51.425 --> 00:01:53.813
studies crying and has
found that women cry

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.892
on average 30 to 64 times a year,

00:01:56.892 --> 00:02:00.944
compared to men who cry A,
three to four times a year,

00:02:00.944 --> 00:02:04.768
B, six to 17 times a year,
C, eight to 10 times a year,

00:02:04.768 --> 00:02:06.667
or D, five to eight times a year.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.488
- Me knowing me, probably three to four.

00:02:08.488 --> 00:02:11.149
- If we're going based
off of like, what men say,

00:02:11.149 --> 00:02:13.673
I'm gonna say five to eight times a year.

00:02:13.673 --> 00:02:14.608
- Probably eight to ten.

00:02:14.608 --> 00:02:15.441
- Final answer?

00:02:15.441 --> 00:02:16.274
- Yes.

00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:17.107
(buzzer sound)

00:02:17.107 --> 00:02:19.160
- It is six to 17 times a year.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.460
- What's wrong with me?

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.293
- Yeah, I believe that.

00:02:21.293 --> 00:02:22.190
- I think it's more than that.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.592
- Guess they probably cry
more but don't cop to it,

00:02:24.592 --> 00:02:25.928
or they like, black it out,

00:02:25.928 --> 00:02:28.497
or they don't think of it as like, crying.

00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:30.487
- Last year was the last
time you cried. (laughs)

00:02:30.487 --> 00:02:31.481
- That's what I'm gonna tell you.

00:02:31.481 --> 00:02:32.314
(laughs)

00:02:32.314 --> 00:02:33.398
- True or false.

00:02:33.398 --> 00:02:36.545
This 1999 study of 81 participants

00:02:36.545 --> 00:02:39.653
from Harvard Medical School
and Boston Children's Hospital

00:02:39.653 --> 00:02:43.046
found that six-month-old boys
were more emotive than girls.

00:02:43.046 --> 00:02:43.879
- I say true.

00:02:43.879 --> 00:02:44.712
- I would say true.

00:02:44.712 --> 00:02:45.545
- I'm gonna say true.

00:02:45.545 --> 00:02:46.768
- You is right, Jared!

00:02:46.768 --> 00:02:47.754
- (whooping) I knew that, knew it.

00:02:47.754 --> 00:02:48.587
- Yay!

00:02:48.587 --> 00:02:50.612
- I have a three year old
boy who lives under me

00:02:50.612 --> 00:02:52.399
and that guy is like, so emotional.

00:02:52.399 --> 00:02:55.592
- A 2011 study from the
University of Missouri

00:02:55.592 --> 00:02:58.529
found that boys do not
discuss feelings because

00:02:58.529 --> 00:03:01.072
A, they are afraid to
talk about their feelings,

00:03:01.072 --> 00:03:03.022
B, they think it will make them look weak,

00:03:03.022 --> 00:03:06.152
C, they are biologically
wired to not feel the need

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.433
to express emotions,

00:03:07.433 --> 00:03:09.096
or D, they don't think it's useful?

00:03:09.096 --> 00:03:09.929
- I would say B.

00:03:09.929 --> 00:03:10.835
- Definitely B.

00:03:10.835 --> 00:03:11.668
- They don't think it's useful.

00:03:11.668 --> 00:03:12.942
- Well, you should have went with your gut

00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:14.265
'cause it's actually D.

00:03:14.265 --> 00:03:16.711
- Yeah, Rocco, yeah Rocco!
- Yeah!

00:03:16.711 --> 00:03:17.544
(laughs)
That's how I feel,

00:03:17.544 --> 00:03:18.895
I'm like, who cares.

00:03:18.895 --> 00:03:20.742
- The writeup on the study was that men

00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:23.401
are more likely to think
talking about problems

00:03:23.401 --> 00:03:25.943
will make the problems feel
bigger than what they are,

00:03:25.943 --> 00:03:28.230
so instead of talking
about them, they'll engage

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.508
in activities to take
their mind off of them.

00:03:30.508 --> 00:03:31.623
- That's definitely not me.

00:03:31.623 --> 00:03:33.266
For me, it's just like,
I don't wanna look weak.

00:03:33.266 --> 00:03:36.199
- The same study also said
that women have a habit

00:03:36.199 --> 00:03:37.801
of over-talking their feelings

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.854
that can produce more
anxiety and stress, so.

00:03:40.854 --> 00:03:42.366
- I know what you're talkin' about.

00:03:42.366 --> 00:03:43.199
(laughs)

00:03:43.199 --> 00:03:45.199
- Oh, really now, Jared!

00:03:46.487 --> 00:03:48.800
- Emotions are a burden,
I don't got time for that.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.946
- I feel like we need to
learn how to cultivate a world

00:03:51.946 --> 00:03:54.582
in which it's not
necessarily being a burden,

00:03:54.582 --> 00:03:56.068
but it's like, you know, I care about you

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:58.921
I wanna make sure you're doin' the best.

00:03:58.921 --> 00:03:59.754
- Yeah!

00:03:59.754 --> 00:04:01.572
And I just want us both
to be able to equally

00:04:01.572 --> 00:04:03.894
communicate that to each other, you know?

00:04:03.894 --> 00:04:05.118
How do you think that we can move towards

00:04:05.118 --> 00:04:07.669
that kind of world,
like especially for men?

00:04:07.669 --> 00:04:10.643
- We gotta promote self care more.

00:04:10.643 --> 00:04:12.813
- I think it's important for men,

00:04:12.813 --> 00:04:16.986
and for anyone who's
struggling with emoting,

00:04:16.986 --> 00:04:19.738
to know that it's not a sign of weakness.

00:04:19.738 --> 00:04:21.538
- I think we gotta
continue raising our kids

00:04:21.538 --> 00:04:24.128
and telling them, hey,
listen, it's okay to cry.

00:04:24.128 --> 00:04:25.190
It takes courage.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:26.502
- I love a good cry.

00:04:26.502 --> 00:04:27.826
Like a nice, like, solid...

00:04:27.826 --> 00:04:28.818
'Cause then you just get it all out.

00:04:28.818 --> 00:04:29.792
All that pent up

00:04:29.792 --> 00:04:31.392
energy and emotion, yeah.
- Get it all the way out.

00:04:31.392 --> 00:04:32.583
- Yeah, drink it up sometimes.

00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:33.416
(laughs)

00:04:33.416 --> 00:04:34.583
- Drink it up!

